(7356814, 1150360, 38032, '<td valign="top">Great image with great color. Feels like it needs  a rotation.<br/>Like this?  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1151849" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/38032/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1151849.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/38032/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1151849.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/38032/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1151849.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Edit to add: the border, while ppl commented on it, IMHO wasn''t a major flaw -- but yeah, not a good idea on DPC =)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2015-06-03 07:40:09.</i></td>', 'Great image with great color. Feels like it needs  a rotation.Like this?    Edit to add: the border, while ppl commented on it, IMHO wasn''t a major flaw -- but yeah, not a good idea on DPC =)', '2015-06-03 08:39:01.000000', '2015-06-03 08:40:09.000000', 0),
(7356833, 1150555, 138253, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BrennanOB:</b></div><hr/><i> There was no filter used in these shots, I just squeezed the aperature way down (F/32 here) as far as I could and that gives you a line of burst for each blade in the lens. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That''s awesome to know, I have had this happen in my images before, but did not know how to explain it. Thanks!</td>', 'Originally posted by BrennanOB: There was no filter used in these shots, I just squeezed the aperature way down (F/32 here) as far as I could and that gives you a line of burst for each blade in the lens.   That''s awesome to know, I have had this happen in my images before, but did not know how to explain it. Thanks!', '2015-06-03 09:26:25.000000', NULL, 0),
